{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ברתמה", :translit "ritmah", :gloss "Rithmah"} {:he "ע\"ש המרגלים", :translit "al shem hameraglim", :gloss "named after the spies"} {:he "שנאמר חצי גבור שנונים עם גחלי רתמים", :translit "shene'emar hetzi gibbor shenunim im gachlei ritmah", :gloss "as stated: half a mighty man sharpened arrows with coals of broom"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name linked to spies via the word ritmah (broom coals) cited from Psalms 120:4"}], :frame {:text "Rithmah is identified as the wilderness station linked to the spies' mission, since the Rithmah desert is where Israel camped when the spies were sent (Rashi on Numbers 33:18, citing Sifrei Zuta 33:18). The verse 'sharpened arrows of a mighty man with coals of broom (gachlei ritmah)' is from Psalms 120:4. The psalm describes deceitful tongues punished as burning coals of broom-wood — a tradition applied to the spies' evil report which inflamed the people against the Land of Israel.", :sources ["Psalms 120:4" "Rashi on Numbers 33:18" "Sifrei Zuta 33:18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name linked to spies via the word ritmah (broom coals) cited from Psalms 120:4", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:45.205284957Z", :model "glm-5.2"}